{
  "_comment": [
    "Hand-written plugins.json, used by checks.genflake-golden as its second input (see the",
    "plan's §3.6). This is a shape resolve.lua cannot currently emit -- one plugin carrying",
    "`commit`, `resolvedRef`, `tag` and `branch` all at once -- so it is written directly rather",
    "than generated: there is no regeneration procedure for this file (contrast",
    "golden/matrix.plugins.json and golden/{matrix,priority}.flake.nix, all of which are",
    "generated -- see docs/plans/29-genflake-golden.md §3.9). This file is never diffed against",
    "anything; only golden/priority.flake.nix, genflake.lua's output from reading it, is.",
    "It exists solely to pin input_url's (lua/nvimx/genflake.lua:33-76) precedence: one ladder",
    "on the github side (commit > resolvedRef > tag > branch), and two independent slots on the",
    "git side (rev: commit > 40-hex resolvedRef; ref: symbolic resolvedRef > tag > branch).",
    "Every field below that is not the plugin's winning field exists only to lose: gh-commit's",
    "resolvedRef/tag/branch, gh-resolved's tag/branch, gh-tag's branch, git-commit's resolvedRef,",
    "git-symbolic's tag, and git-symbolic/git-tag's branch. Together they force one total order",
    "across the ladder; individually some are redundant with another plugin's field, but which",
    "ones are redundant shifts whenever the ladder changes, so never delete one just because it",
    "is not the winner for its own plugin -- that is exactly the regression they exist to catch.",
    "If plugins.json's schema grows, this file has to be updated by hand: genflake.lua only",
    "reads a handful of keys, so a new key would otherwise pass through silently unexercised."
  ],
